    "title": "I-75 SB down to 2 lanes near Campbell Road - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Southall ,\n6 hours ago\nSIDNEY, Ohio ( WDTN ) – In the late hours of Tuesday, July 14, workers began reconstruction of a bridge alongside I-75 at Campbell Road in Shelby County.\nStarting on Wednesday, I-75 SB will be downgraded to two lanes, with lanes expected to remain closed until the end of this year.\nThe traffic shift will allow crews to remove and replace the bridge deck in the right lane on I-75 South.\nAnyone traveling during the construction period is asked to use caution and allow for any extra time the closure may add to the commute.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
    "summary": "SIDNEY, Ohio ( WDTN ) – In the late hours of Tuesday, July 14, workers began reconstruction of a bridge alongside I-75 at Campbell Road in Shelby County. The traffic shift will allow crews to remove and replace the bridge deck in the right lane on I-75 South. Anyone traveling during the construction period is asked to use caution and allow for any extra time the closure may add to the commute. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
